  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.087,
            0.901,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen in the chapter on ‘Life Processes’ that the food we eat is digested by various enzymes in our body. Have you ever wondered why the same enzyme does not break-down everything we eat? Enzymes are specific in their action, specific enzymes are needed for the break-down of a particular substance. That is why we will not get any energy if we try to eat coal! Because of this, many human-made materials like plastics will not be broken down by the action of bacteria or other saprophytes. These materials will be acted upon by physical processes like heat and pressure, but under the ambient conditions found in our environment, these persist for a long time.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.265,
            0.9,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Substances that are broken down by biological processes are said to be biodegradable. How many of the substances you buried were biodegradable? Substances that are not broken down in this manner are said to be non-biodegradable. These substances may be inert and simply persist in the environment for a long time or may harm the various members of the eco-system.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.31,
            0.4,
            0.482,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 13.6"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.437,
            0.874,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use the library or internet to find out more about biodegradable and non-biodegradable substances.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.466,
            0.874,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How long are various non-biodegradable substances expected to last in our environment?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.495,
            0.875,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These days, new types of plastics which are said to be biodegradable are available. Find out more about such materials and whether they do or do not harm the environment.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.585,
            0.744,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q U E S T I O N S"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.633,
            0.752,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Why are some substances biodegradable and some non-biodegradable?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.655,
            0.752,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Give any two ways in which biodegradable substances would affect the environment.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.789,
            0.631,
            0.849,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
